---
const layers = [
  {
    name: 'App (UI)',
    detail: 'Avalonia window, themes, settings, orchestration',
    color: 'from-ntilde-500 to-ntilde-700',
  },
  {
    name: 'Platform',
    detail: 'Input, paths, process, SSH — shared runtime primitives',
    color: 'from-ntilde-600 to-ntilde-800',
  },
  {
    name: 'VT',
    detail: 'Frame-agnostic parser + cell-based buffer (zero references)',
    color: 'from-ntilde-400 to-ntilde-600',
  },
  {
    name: 'Rendering',
    detail: 'SkiaSharp text shaping, GPU glyph cache, snapshot boundary',
    color: 'from-ntilde-500 to-ntilde-700',
  },
  {
    name: 'Pty',
    detail: 'OS integration + PTY sessions (raw bytes only, no VT)',
    color: 'from-ntilde-600 to-ntilde-800',
  },
  {
    name: 'Replay',
    detail: 'Deterministic session recording and playback',
    color: 'from-ntilde-400 to-ntilde-600',
  },
];

const flows = [
  {
    title: 'Bytes become cells',
    body:
      'The PTY layer delivers raw bytes from the shell. The VT parser turns them into typed cells in a frame-agnostic buffer. The renderer snapshots that buffer at frame boundaries — never more often.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Snapshots stay pixel-stable',
    body:
      'Rendering is gated by a performance contract: same buffer state, same pixels, every time. Replay parity is a first-class test, not a best-effort log.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Conformance is enforced',
    body:
      'A dedicated CI lane regenerates the VT/ANSI conformance report on every change and fails on regressions. Ghostty gap tracking keeps the matrix honest.',
  },
];
---

<section
  id="how-it-works"
  class="section border-b border-ink-900/60"
  aria-labelledby="how-title"
>
  <div class="container-prose">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2
        id="how-title"
        class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl"
      >
        A small, acyclic core. A wide, replaceable surface.
      </h2>
      <p class="lede mt-4 max-w-2xl">
        Ntilde is organized into focused class libraries with an
        acyclic dependency graph. The architecture invariants are
        <span class="text-white">enforced</span> by
        <code class="rounded bg-ink-800/60 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-ntilde-200">Ntilde.Architecture.Tests</code> at IL, csproj, and namespace level — not aspirational.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <h3
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-400"
        >
          Module graph
        </h3>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2.5" role="list">
          {
            layers.map((layer, i) => (
              <li
                class="flex items-center gap-4 rounded-lg border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900/40 p-4"
              >
                <span
                  class={
                    'grid h-9 w-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-md bg-gradient-to-br text-ink-950 font-mono text-sm font-semibold ' +
                    layer.color
                  }
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
                </span>
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <p class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-white">
                    {layer.name}
                  </p>
                  <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-400">
                    {layer.detail}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-500">
          Enforced invariants: <code class="text-ntilde-300">VT</code> is a leaf
          with zero project references;
          <code class="text-ntilde-300">Pty</code> must <em>not</em> depend on
          <code class="text-ntilde-300">VT</code>;
          <code class="text-ntilde-300">Replay</code> and
          <code class="text-ntilde-300">Rendering</code> reference exactly
          <code class="text-ntilde-300">VT</code>; no production assembly
          references test libraries.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <h3
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-400"
        >
          Data flow
        </h3>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-4" role="list">
          {
            flows.map((flow, i) => (
              <li class="card">
                <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white">
                  <span
                    class="grid h-5 w-5 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ntilde-500/15 font-mono text-[10px] text-ntilde-300"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  >
                    {i + 1}
                  </span>
                  {flow.title}
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-300">
                  {flow.body}
                </p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
